{"c": null, "r": "I'm designing a Bank class with account management methods—opening accounts, depositing, withdrawing, checking balances, and transferring between accounts. I need to handle validation: deposits and withdrawals require positive amounts, initial balances can't be negative, and the amount parameter itself must be an integer. For error handling, I'm raising KeyError for unknown accounts and ValueError for duplicate account names or negative initial balances.

For transfers, I'm adding checks to ensure both source and destination accounts exist, the amounts are positive, and the source has sufficient funds. The legacy module functions will delegate to a default Bank instance, and I'll pass through the `initial` parameter with a default of 0. Unknown accounts in deposits should raise KeyError from the dictionary lookup, matching the original behavior.
", "t": [["write_file", "{"path":"D:\\Projects\\local_ai\\strata-lab\\runs\\work\\hermes\\bank-1794053343\\bank.py","content":"\"\"\"Account helpers. Balances are integer cents.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass InsufficientFunds(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when a withdrawal or transfer exceeds the source balance.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass Bank:\n    \"\"\"A set of named accounts with integer-cent balances.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._accounts = {}\n\n    def open_account(self, name, initial=0):\n        if name in self._accounts:\n            raise ValueError(\"account exists: \" + name)\n        if initial < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"initial balance must be >= 0, got \" + repr(initial))\n        self._accounts[name] = initial\n\n    def deposit(self, name, amount):\n        if amount <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"amount must be > 0, got \" + repr(amount))\n        if name not in self._accounts:\n            raise KeyError(name)\n        self._accounts[name] += amount\n\n    def withdraw(self, name, amount):\n        if amount <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"amount must be > 0, got \" + repr(amount))\n        if name not in self._accounts:\n            raise KeyError(name)\n        current = self._accounts[name]\n        if current < amount:\n            raise InsufficientFunds(\n                \"account %r has %d, cannot withdraw %d\" % (name, current, amount)\n            )\n        self._accounts[name] = current - amount\n\n    def balance(self, name):\n        if name not in self._accounts:\n            raise KeyError(name)\n        return self._accounts[name]\n\n    def transfer(self, src, dst, amount):\n        if amount <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"amount must be > 0, got \" + repr(amount))\n        if src not in self._accounts:\n            raise KeyError(src)\n        if dst not in self._accounts:\n            raise KeyError(dst)\n        if src == dst:\n            raise ValueError(\"cannot transfer to the same account: \" + src)\n        current = self._accounts[src]\n        if current < amount:\n            raise InsufficientFunds(\n                \"account %r has %d, cannot transfer %d to %r\"\n                % (src, current, amount, dst)\n            )\n        self._accounts[src] = current - amount\n        self._accounts[dst] += amount\n\n\ndefault_bank = Bank()\n\n\ndef open_account(name, initial=0):\n    default_bank.open_account(name, initial)\n\n\ndef deposit(name, amount):\n    default_bank.deposit(name, amount)\n\n\ndef withdraw(name, amount):\n    default_bank.withdraw(name, amount)\n\n\ndef balance(name):\n    return default_bank.balance(name)\n\n\ndef transfer(src, dst, amount):\n    default_bank.transfer(src, dst, amount)\n"}"]]}
